Recommends: pipewire-pulse | pulseaudio,
Description: play and record meetings, and read along with their transcripts
 Cassini plays meeting recordings in the Cassini portable meeting format:
 ordinary Ogg Opus files that carry their own word-by-word transcript,
 speaker names and summary.
 .
 It highlights the spoken word as the recording plays, lets you click any
 word to play from there, see participants, search the transcript, read the
 summary, verify that the audio matches its transcript, and export the
 transcript as text or WebVTT subtitles.
 .
 Cassini also records meetings. It captures the microphone and desktop audio
 into an Opus file through a PulseAudio-compatible sound server such as
 PipeWire. With its companion extension for Chromium-based browsers, which
 this package includes together with the extension's native messaging
 hosts, it records each audio source of a WebRTC meeting on its own track.
